# Local patterns

Yours. Written by your engagements, read alongside `patterns.md` before every
run. This file exists so that pulling upstream never conflicts with what your
own runs have learned — upstream owns `patterns.md`, you own this one.

**Same rules as `patterns.md`.** Patterns only: never flags, never credentials,
never anything specific to one machine that a future run cannot use. If an entry
only describes what happened on one box, it belongs in that engagement's
`WRITEUP.md` instead.

It is gitignored by default so nothing leaves your machine by accident.
`pwnloop ship` force-adds it when you choose to push, so forks can keep their
learnings in their own repository.

**Found something that generalises beyond your lab?** Open a pull request moving
that entry from here into `patterns.md`. That is how the shared methodology
improves from other people's engagements and not only mine.

